    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20-a1">

                <pb facs="0066" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg800"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 91—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Marcelin to Mr. Terres.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State for Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                4, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vice-Consul-General</hi>: I regret to have to
                    announce to you that the department of the interior and of the general police,
                    in view of the conduct of Mr. Eugene Wiener, an American citizen, resident of
                    Jeremie, has issued against him a decree of expulsion, together with the citizen
                    Yolny Dermonzy, of French nationality.</p>
                <p>I hand to you inclosed copy of the decree, in which you will find the causes
                    which have been the motive of that decision.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Marcelin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State ad interim for Foreign
                            Relations.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
